# Charter code ownership.
#
# The maintainer owns everything. The explicit entries below are not
# redundant: they exist so that a future change to the catch-all rule, or an
# added team, cannot accidentally leave a sensitive path unreviewed. The last
# matching pattern wins, so ordering matters -- broad first, sensitive last.
#
# Spec section 15 requires CODEOWNERS on migration directories, so engineer approval of
# a schema change is structurally required rather than a Charter-side policy.
# Spec section 7.4 and section 26.10 put the merge gate outside Charter entirely; these
# entries plus branch protection are what enforce it.

# Everything.
*                                   @binn

# Legal and licensing. Changing any of these changes the terms the project is
# offered under (spec section 24).
/LICENSE                            @binn
/CLA.md                             @binn
/TRADEMARK.md                       @binn
/SECURITY.md                        @binn
/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md                 @binn

# CI, release, and the agent-session workflow. A change here can exfiltrate
# secrets or publish an image.
/.github/                           @binn
/.github/workflows/                 @binn
/.github/CODEOWNERS                 @binn

# Database migrations -- spec section 15. Destructive and ambiguous migrations must
# never merge without the maintainer.
**/Migrations/                      @binn
**/Migrations/**                    @binn

# Auth, identity, and authorisation. Spec section 7, section 21.
/src/Charter/Auth/                  @binn
/src/Charter/Authorization/         @binn
/src/Charter/Identity/              @binn
**/Auth/**                          @binn
**/Authorization/**                 @binn

# Credential storage and encryption. Spec section 20b.2.
/src/Charter/Credentials/           @binn
**/Credentials/**                   @binn

# The runner boundary. Path scope and token scoping are enforced here, not in
# the UI (spec section 7.3, section 7.4).
/src/Charter/Runners/               @binn
/src/Charter.Agent/                 @binn
/src/Charter.DetachedRunner/        @binn
/runners/                           @binn

# Configuration parsing and startup validation. Spec section 4.
/src/Charter/Configuration/         @binn
/Directory.Build.props              @binn
/Dockerfile                         @binn
/docker-compose.yml                 @binn
/.env.example                       @binn

# Agent guidance and the specification.
/AGENTS.md                          @binn
/CLAUDE.md                          @binn
/agent-docs/                        @binn
/.claude/                           @binn
